{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_014oqidjkLGeqvr5n7CYuJhd","type":"tool_result","content":"db5b95bf chore(pose): bind the ires matrix to its review\n5bfc126d chore(pose): index the ires matrix\n44a748f0 chore(pose): record the ires matrix\nc7b37912 chore(pose): index the ires round r3 fixes\n53e9f889 fix(pose): name scope changes from the root and keep those outside it\n8cd779f3 chore(pose): record review round 2 of the index-reads residuals\n0015e36e chore(pose): index the ires binding\ndiff --git a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\nindex 16a5c0ca..eb80566d 100644\n--- a/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\n+++ b/.pose/specs/2026-11-27-pose-validate-index-reads-residuals.md\n@@ -34,9 +34,9 @@ Reopening the decisions of the origin spec.\n ### Functional\n - R1: With the POSE root below the repository top, the ready-transition read shall list changed specs (Git names them top-relative), so their ready transitions are checked (round 1 N11, round 5 N3).\n - R2: The versioned report shall carry no absolute path of the checkout when the change list cannot be read: it states that the list could not be read, and the warning on standard error carries Git's message (round 5, N1; D1).\n-- R3: The bounds on Git's message and the report note shall cut at a character, never inside a UTF-8 sequence (round 5, N4).\n+- R3: The bound on Git's message shall cut at a character, never inside a UTF-8 sequence (round 5, N4).\n - R4: A failing `ls-files` in worktree scope selection shall fail the selection with its cause instead of silently dropping untracked files (round 5, N5).\n-- R5: The guards listed by rounds 2–5 shall each have a failing test: restoring `--path-format`, the `X^-` cut, the report note bound and stderr warning, `GitEnglish` on the check, lookup and hand-over, the memfd write fallback, the private copy keeping the index's time, a stand-in Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format`, and a locale test independent of installed translations; the ledger's context is L1 (rounds 1 N6–N7, 2 N16, 3 N21, 5 N2).\n+- R5: The guards listed by rounds 2–5 shall each have a failing test: restoring `--path-format`, the `X^-` cut, the report's stderr warning, `GitEnglish` on the check, lookup and hand-over, the memfd write fallback, the private copy keeping the index's time, a stand-in Git that echoes an unknown `--path-format`, and a locale test independent of installed translations; the ledger's context is L1 (rounds 1 N6–N7, 2 N16, 3 N21, 5 N2).\n \n ### Non-functional\n Existing behaviour outside the stated requirements is unchanged.\n@@ -109,6 +109,7 @@ Each requirement gets a regression test shown failing before its code.\n ### Execution log\n - 2026-11-27: R1 adds `--relative` to the ready-transition diff; R2 replaces the root, repository top, Git directories, temporary and home directories whole before the generic pattern, which now also starts after `:`, a backtick or `[`; R3 cuts at a character (`TruncateUTF8`); R4 fails scope selection on a failed untracked listing; R5 adds stand-in Git tests. Each guard fails its test mutated out: `TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop`, `TestTheReportStatesNoPath`, `TestBoundsCutAtACharacter`, `TestScopeSelectionReportsAFailedUntrackedListing`, `TestTheIndexLookupNeedsNoPathFormat`, `TestIndexReadsRunGitInEnglish`, `TestTheIndexFallbacksKeepTheAnswer`, `TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards`.\n - 2026-11-27: the first matrix failed `release-test-compile-darwin` and `-windows`: a test used the Linux-only memfd hooks; it moved to the Linux test file. Review round 1 (rrn-977f027e0e7c7ee5) requested changes. N1: the ready transition reads HEAD's text with `HEAD:./`, relative to the root, so a spec in progress at HEAD below the repository top is not a new transition. N2–N6: the redaction is withdrawn (D1). N7: scope selection runs its diff with `--relative`. `TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop` and `TestTheReportStatesNoPath` fail with `HEAD:./`, `--relative` or the note mutated.\n+- 2026-11-27: review round 2 (rrn-3dba382397f270c7) requested changes: `--relative` dropped changes outside the root, narrowing validation (N1). Withdrawn: the diff names changes from the repository top, and each is named from the root (`scopeRootRelative`): inside it without the prefix, outside it as `../<name>`, a change outside every module that selects the root. The test changes a tracked file at the top and fails with either branch mutated out. N3: R3 and R5 no longer name the removed note bound, and the bounded-note assertion is gone. N4: the report warning test requires Git's message. N2 is a follow-up.\n \n ### Results summary\n The full `pose-mcp` suite passes; the canonical result is refreshed with `pose validate --carry`.\n@@ -138,4 +139,5 @@ Ready transitions and scope selection see a root below the repository top; the r\n L1 above.\n \n ### Follow-ups\n-None. Origin: `pose-validate-read-only-index-followups` (done 2026-11-27).\n+Origin: `pose-validate-read-only-index-followups` (done 2026-11-27).\n+- [open] Name carry exclusions and the `show <head>:<path>` reads of carry from the root, as scope selection now does, for when carry runs below the repository top (review round 2, N2). (owner:@pose-maintainers crit:low review:2026-12-27)\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\nindex bfc6acbd..16594b7d 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\n@@ -300,8 +300,9 @@ func readLastReportRecord(path string) *reportRecord {\n // reportChangedFilesNoted is reportChangedFiles for the report: outside a\n // repository Git can open at all the plain listing stays silent, as before\n // (review round 1, N9; round 3, N19);\n-// any other failure is returned to warn about and stated in the list, on\n-// one line (review round 2, N12, N15).\n+// any other failure is returned to warn about, with Git's message, while the\n+// list states only that it could not be read (spec\n+// pose-validate-index-reads-residuals D1).\n func reportChangedFilesNoted(root, since string, locale cliLocale) ([]string, error) {\n \tfiles, err := reportChangedFiles(root, since)\n \tif err == nil {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\nindex 750bd771..c15e622a 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_index_residuals_test.go\n@@ -84,6 +84,23 @@ func TestReadyTransitionsSeeSpecsBelowTheRepositoryTop(t *testing.T) {\n \tif err != nil || len(sel.Changed) != 2 || sel.Changed[1] != \"x.txt\" || strings.HasPrefix(strings.Join(sel.Changed, \",\"), \"proj/\") {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"scope selection below the repository top: %v %v\", sel.Changed, err)\n \t}\n+\t// Review round 2, N1: a change outside the root is kept, as a change\n+\t// outside every module, so it widens the selection instead of vanishing.\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(top, \"outside.txt\"), []byte(\"o\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tfor _, args := range [][]string{{\"add\", \"-A\"}, {\"-c\", \"user.name=t\", \"-c\", \"user.email=t@t\", \"commit\", \"-q\", \"-m\", \"outside\"}} {\n+\t\tif out, err := exec.Command(\"git\", append([]string{\"-C\", top}, args...)...).CombinedOutput(); err != nil {\n+\t\t\tt.Fatal(args, err, string(out))\n+\t\t}\n+\t}\n+\tif err := os.WriteFile(filepath.Join(top, \"outside.txt\"), []byte(\"changed\\n\"), 0o644); err != nil {\n+\t\tt.Fatal(err)\n+\t}\n+\tsel, err = computeChangedScopeWith(root, \"HEAD\", \"\", nil, scopeMetadata{})\n+\tif err != nil || !strings.Contains(strings.Join(sel.Changed, \",\"), \"../outside.txt\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"a change outside the root vanished: %v %v\", sel.Changed, err)\n+\t}\n }\n \n // R2: the versioned report carries no message of Git, so no path of the\n@@ -126,12 +143,10 @@ func TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards(t *testing.T) {\n \t\tt.Fatalf(\"the check's listing did not run in English: %s\", out)\n \t}\n \n-\tfiles, err := reportChangedFilesNoted(root, \"\", localeEN)\n-\tif err == nil || len(files) != 1 || len(files[0]) > 700 {\n-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the report note is not bounded: %d bytes, %v\", len(strings.Join(files, \"\")), err)\n-\t}\n-\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"report\", \"--task\", \"residual check\"); code != 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"the changed files cannot be listed\") {\n-\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the report did not warn: %d %s\", code, out)\n+\t// The warning on standard error carries Git's message (D1; review round\n+\t// 2, N4).\n+\tif code, out := runPose(t, root, \"report\", \"--task\", \"residual check\"); code != 0 || !strings.Contains(out, \"the changed files cannot be listed\") || !strings.Contains(out, \"no status here\") {\n+\t\tt.Fatalf(\"the report did not warn with Git's message: %d %s\", code, out)\n \t}\n \tindex := filepath.Join(root, \".git\", \"index\")\n \tif err := os.Remove(index); err != nil {\ndiff --git a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\nindex fc750c39..3684d7f8 100644\n--- a/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n+++ b/pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\n@@ -99,9 +99,7 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \t// keeps its owner, and a rename names both its source and its destination\n \t// (review round 2, N1 and N3).\n \t// Configuration never hides a changed gitlink (review round 8, N23).\n-\t// --relative: with the root below the repository top Git names changes\n-\t// top-relative otherwise, and no module owns them (review round 1, N7).\n-\tgitArgs := []string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"diff.ignoreSubmodules=none\", \"diff\", \"--relative\", \"--ignore-submodules=none\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"--no-renames\", base}\n+\tgitArgs := []string{\"-C\", root, \"-c\", \"diff.ignoreSubmodules=none\", \"diff\", \"--ignore-submodules=none\", \"--name-only\", \"-z\", \"--no-renames\", base}\n \tif head != \"\" {\n \t\tgitArgs = append(gitArgs, head)\n \t}\n@@ -112,9 +110,14 @@ func computeChangedScopeWith(root, base, head string, modules []validationModule\n \tif err != nil {\n \t\treturn sel, scopeDiffError(root, base, head, sel.rangeLabel(), err)\n \t}\n+\t// Git names changes from the repository top. With the root below it, a\n+\t// change inside the root is named from the root, so its module owns it,\n+\t// and one outside stays a change outside every module, which selects the\n+\t// root, never nothing (review rounds 1 N7, 2 N1).\n+\tprefix := scopeRootPrefix(root)\n \tfor _, name := range strings.Split(string(out), \"\\x00\") {\n \t\tif name != \"\" {\n-\t\t\tsel.Changed = append(sel.Changed, filepath.ToSlash(name))\n+\t\t\tsel.Changed = append(sel.Changed, scopeRootRelative(prefix, filepath.ToSlash(name)))\n \t\t}\n \t}\n \tif head == \"\" {\n@@ -309,3 +312,25 @@ func scopeRevisions(base, head string) []string {\n \t}\n \treturn revs\n }\n+\n+// scopeRootPrefix is the root's path from the repository top, with a trailing\n+// slash, or \"\" at the top.\n+func scopeRootPrefix(root string) string {\n+\tout, err := posemodel.RawGit(\"-C\", root, \"rev-parse\", \"--show-prefix\").Output()\n+\tif err != nil {\n+\t\treturn \"\"\n+\t}\n+\treturn strings.TrimSpace(string(out))\n+}\n+\n+// scopeRootRelative names a top-relative path from the root: inside it\n+// without the prefix, outside it as ../ plus its top-relative name.\n+func scopeRootRelative(prefix, name string) string {\n+\tif prefix == \"\" {\n+\t\treturn name\n+\t}\n+\tif rest, ok := strings.CutPrefix(name, prefix); ok {\n+\t\treturn rest\n+\t}\n+\treturn \"../\" + name\n+}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"[private-session]","uuid":"d39a6701-92f4-4ca4-bb55-320b4c6e2203","timestamp":"2026-11-27T18:59:41.859Z","tool_use_re