{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTzPmAVcSF5tga3h9xXV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XAE8cpTczFMRg5xQQHQShp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"printf '%s\\n' 'decision: changes-requested' '```pose-draft' '{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",' '\"findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":102,\"summary\":\"Regression: the diff does not pin diff.relative, and the new naming assumes top-relative output. With the root below the top and diff.relative=true in Git config, a change to proj/mod/x.txt is named ../mod/x.txt and the self-contained module that owns it is not selected, with no error; the base engine selected it (reproduced against both versions). In that configuration a tracked change outside the root is also still dropped, changed=[], as at base. Validation narrows silently. Reach: only a root below the repository top, which the shipped CLI does not pass (it resolves the top).\"},' '{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":323,\"summary\":\"scopeRootPrefix trims all surrounding space, so below a directory with a leading space every change is named as outside and its self-contained module is not selected (reproduced; base did not select it either). By reading, a failing rev-parse also returns an empty prefix silently, which restores the R1-N7 misnaming.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":335,\"summary\":\"An outside change is named ../ plus its top-relative name, which is root-relative only for a root one level down. With root a/b, a/c/f.txt becomes ../a/c/f.txt, so a self-contained module declaring ../c is not selected (reproduced; base did not select it either). The spec API section says names are relative to the root and records no decision on this outside form.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":128,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing: ls-files runs under the root, so below the top a new untracked file outside the root is not listed and nothing is selected for it (reproduced, same at base), unlike a tracked outside change.\"},' '{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":314,\"summary\":\"Rest of R2-N3: report.go:314-317 still describes a bounded line with absolute paths removed, and the comment at validate_index_residuals_test.go:134 still says the report bounds its note.\"}' '],' '\"prior_findings\":[' '{\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"With default config a change under a lower root is named from it and its module selected (overlay probe: mod/x.txt selects mod). With diff.relative=true the module is again not selected; see N1.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N1\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"With default config an outside change is kept and selects root and non-self-contained modules (probe: ../shared.txt selects . and mod); the test fails with the round 2 validate_scope.go overlaid. With diff.relative=true it still vanishes, as at base; see N1.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N2\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_carry.go is unchanged since round 2; the spec Follow-ups section records it as open, low, review 2026-12-27.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"R3, R5 and the vacuous assertion are cleaned in the diff a73f371a..db5b95bf; stale comments remain at report.go:314 and validate_index_residuals_test.go:134 (N5).\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N4\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards now requires the stand-in text no status here in the pose report output; it passes in the focused run.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"The round 3 delta line by line and the whole range as it bears on it: scope naming and its consumers (selection, declared dependencies, exclusions, counts), report note and comments, changed tests, amended spec; focused tests and go vet, a round 2 overlay, base and head probes over lower roots, diff.relative, outside and untracked changes, nested and spaced directories, and every planned pose tool including both validate runs.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"The naming assumes Git always prints top-relative names, which diff.relative changes. L1 was read and is not disputed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The delta adds one read-only rev-parse and no shared state; the concurrent index-read test is in the focused run, which passed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No schema or tool contract changes; at the repository top names are unchanged because the prefix is empty.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions stay validated and a failed untracked listing fails with its cause. The silent prefix fallback is low, in N2.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The report warning carries the Git message and a test now requires it.\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"Nothing differs at the top; a lower root with diff.relative selects less than before.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"Naming after the diff, instead of filtering with --relative, addresses the cause of R2-N1, but depends on an output form the command does not fix. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the amended requirements, execution log and follow-up: they match behaviour for the shipped CLI. Leftover wording is N3 and N5.\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Selection errors and the report warning name the failing read and what Git said.\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 to R5 as amended each have a passing focused test; N1 concerns the scope selection fix, which no requirement states.\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The nine code files match the spec artifact list; the lower-root selection change answers earlier findings and is stated in the spec API section and log.\"},' '{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Changed names, including ../ forms, are only matched as strings in the code read, never opened; the versioned report interpolates nothing from Git.\"},' '{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A prefix lookup and a small rename function is proportionate; it holds only while the diff output form is fixed, the condition N1 breaks.\"}' '],' '\"tools\":[' '{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-index-reads-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},' '{\"id\":\"assess-