t selects . and mod); the test fails with the round 2 validate_scope.go overlaid. With diff.relative=true it still vanishes, as at base; see N1.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N2\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_carry.go is unchanged since round 2; the spec Follow-ups section records it as open, low, review 2026-12-27.\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"R3, R5 and the vacuous assertion are cleaned in the diff a73f371a..db5b95bf; stale comments remain at report.go:314 and validate_index_residuals_test.go:134 (N5).\"},' '{\"id\":\"R2-N4\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards now requires the stand-in text no status here in the pose report output; it passes in the focused run.\"}' '],' '\"sweep\":\"The round 3 delta line by line and the whole range as it bears on it: scope naming and its consumers (selection, declared dependencies, exclusions, counts), report note and comments, changed tests, amended spec; focused tests and go vet, a round 2 overlay, base and head probes over lower roots, diff.relative, outside and untracked changes, nested and spaced directories, and every planned pose tool including both validate runs.\",' '\"criteria\":[' '{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"The naming assumes Git always prints top-relative names, which diff.relative changes. L1 was read and is not disputed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The delta adds one read-only rev-parse and no shared state; the concurrent index-read test is in the focused run, which passed.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No schema or tool contract changes; at the repository top names are unchanged because the prefix is empty.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions stay validated and a failed untracked listing fails with its cause. The silent prefix fallback is low, in N2.\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The report warning carries the Git message and a test now requires it.\"},' '{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"Nothing differs at the top; a lower root with diff.relative selects less than before.\"},' '{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},' '{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"Naming after the diff, instead of filtering with --relative, addresses the cause of R2-N1, but depends on an output form the command does not fix. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\"},' '{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the amended requirements, execution log and follow-up: they match behaviour for the shipped CLI. Leftover wording is N3 and N5.\"},' '{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Selection errors and the report warning name the failing read and what Git said.\"},' '{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 to R5 as amended each have a passing focused test; N1 concerns the scope selection fix, which no requirement states.\"},' '{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The nine code files match the spec artifact list; the lower-root selection change answers earlier findings and is stated in the spec API section and log.\"