{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChTzRmHzRcgcYZhLsJGVL","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"decision: changes-requested\n\nOne blocker is left. The round 3 naming fix assumes Git prints paths from the repository top, and the `diff.relative` setting breaks that assumption.\n\n## Findings\n\n| ID | Severity | Disposition | Location | Defect |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| N1 | medium | blocker | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:102` | With the root below the top and `diff.relative=true`, `mod/x.txt` is named `../mod/x.txt` and its self-contained module is not selected. The base engine selected it. |\n| N2 | low | follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:323` | Trimming the prefix breaks directory names with a leading space (reproduced). A failed `rev-parse` also appears to return an empty prefix silently (by reading). |\n| N3 | low | follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:335` | The `../` form of an outside path is only right one level down. With root `a/b`, a declared dependency `../c` is missed. |\n| N4 | low | follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go:128` | Pre-existing: new untracked files outside a lower root are not listed. |\n| N5 | low | follow-up | `pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go:314` | Stale comments about a bounded, redacted report note remain here and at `validate_index_residuals_test.go:134`. |\n\nN1 only affects a root below the repository top, which the shipped CLI never passes.\n\n## Earlier findings\n\n| Finding | Status |\n|---|---|\n| R2-N4 | fixed |\n| R1-N7, R2-N1 | partial: fixed with default Git config, but see N1 |\n| R2-N3 | partial: see N5 |\n| R2-N2 | not fixed; recorded in the spec as an open follow-up |\n\n## Criteria\n\n| Result | Criteria |\n|---|---|\n| finding (N1) | `assumption-integrity`, `backend-integration-impact`, `compatibility`, `correctness`, `design-causality` |\n| passed | `backend-concurrency`, `backend-contracts`, `backend-input-errors`, `backend-observability`, `documentation`, `operability`, `requirements`, `scope`, `security`, `solution-proportionality` |\n\n## What ran\n- **Focused tests:** they passed, and `go vet` on the two packages printed nothing. The below-the-top test fails when the round 2 `validate_scope.go` is put back.\n- **Full validation:** both runs failed in the sandbox. The root run had 224 of 236 steps passing and the module run 221 of 233, with the same failing steps as earlier rounds. Their entries are marked passed on the sealed evidence, with the failure stated.\n- **Accepted limit:** I do not dispute L1.\n- **Cleanup:** `go clean -cache` and the `go-build*` removal exited 0 inside the sandbox. The draft check accepted the block below.\n\n```pose-draft\n{\"schema\":\"pose.review.draft/v1\",\"decision\":\"changes-requested\",\n\"findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"N1\",\"severity\":\"medium\",\"disposition\":\"blocker\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":102,\"summary\":\"Regression: the diff does not pin diff.relative, and the new naming assumes top-relative output. With the root below the top and diff.relative=true in Git config, a change to proj/mod/x.txt is named ../mod/x.txt and the self-contained module that owns it is not selected, with no error; the base engine selected it (reproduced against both versions). In that configuration a tracked change outside the root is also still dropped, changed=[], as at base. Validation narrows silently. Reach: only a root below the repository top, which the shipped CLI does not pass (it resolves the top).\"},\n{\"id\":\"N2\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":323,\"summary\":\"scopeRootPrefix trims all surrounding space, so below a directory with a leading space every change is named as outside and its self-contained module is not selected (reproduced; base did not select it either). By reading, a failing rev-parse also returns an empty prefix silently, which restores the R1-N7 misnaming.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N3\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":335,\"summary\":\"An outside change is named ../ plus its top-relative name, which is root-relative only for a root one level down. With root a/b, a/c/f.txt becomes ../a/c/f.txt, so a self-contained module declaring ../c is not selected (reproduced; base did not select it either). The spec API section says names are relative to the root and records no decision on this outside form.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N4\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/validate_scope.go\",\"line\":128,\"summary\":\"Pre-existing: ls-files runs under the root, so below the top a new untracked file outside the root is not listed and nothing is selected for it (reproduced, same at base), unlike a tracked outside change.\"},\n{\"id\":\"N5\",\"severity\":\"low\",\"disposition\":\"follow-up\",\"file\":\"pose-mcp/internal/cli/report.go\",\"line\":314,\"summary\":\"Rest of R2-N3: report.go:314-317 still describes a bounded line with absolute paths removed, and the comment at validate_index_residuals_test.go:134 still says the report bounds its note.\"}\n],\n\"prior_findings\":[\n{\"id\":\"R1-N7\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"With default config a change under a lower root is named from it and its module selected (overlay probe: mod/x.txt selects mod). With diff.relative=true the module is again not selected; see N1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N1\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"With default config an outside change is kept and selects root and non-self-contained modules (probe: ../shared.txt selects . and mod); the test fails with the round 2 validate_scope.go overlaid. With diff.relative=true it still vanishes, as at base; see N1.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N2\",\"status\":\"not-fixed\",\"evidence\":\"validate_carry.go is unchanged since round 2; the spec Follow-ups section records it as open, low, review 2026-12-27.\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N3\",\"status\":\"partial\",\"evidence\":\"R3, R5 and the vacuous assertion are cleaned in the diff a73f371a..db5b95bf; stale comments remain at report.go:314 and validate_index_residuals_test.go:134 (N5).\"},\n{\"id\":\"R2-N4\",\"status\":\"fixed\",\"evidence\":\"TestTheRemainingIndexReadGuards now requires the stand-in text no status here in the pose report output; it passes in the focused run.\"}\n],\n\"sweep\":\"The round 3 delta line by line and the whole range as it bears on it: scope naming and its consumers (selection, declared dependencies, exclusions, counts), report note and comments, changed tests, amended spec; focused tests and go vet, a round 2 overlay, base and head probes over lower roots, diff.relative, outside and untracked changes, nested and spaced directories, and every planned pose tool including both validate runs.\",\n\"criteria\":[\n{\"id\":\"assumption-integrity\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"The naming assumes Git always prints top-relative names, which diff.relative changes. L1 was read and is not disputed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-concurrency\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The delta adds one read-only rev-parse and no shared state; the concurrent index-read test is in the focused run, which passed.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-contracts\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"No schema or tool contract changes; at the repository top names are unchanged because the prefix is empty.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-input-errors\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Revisions stay validated and a failed untracked listing fails with its cause. The silent prefix fallback is low, in N2.\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-integration-impact\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"backend-observability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The report warning carries the Git message and a test now requires it.\"},\n{\"id\":\"compatibility\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"Nothing differs at the top; a lower root with diff.relative selects less than before.\"},\n{\"id\":\"correctness\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\"},\n{\"id\":\"design-causality\",\"disposition\":\"finding\",\"evidence\":\"N1\",\"rationale\":\"Naming after the diff, instead of filtering with --relative, addresses the cause of R2-N1, but depends on an output form the command does not fix. The design assessment observed no structural deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"documentation\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/distributed-instructions-parity-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Examined the amended requirements, execution log and follow-up: they match behaviour for the shipped CLI. Leftover wording is N3 and N5.\"},\n{\"id\":\"operability\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Selection errors and the report warning name the failing read and what Git said.\"},\n{\"id\":\"requirements\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"R1 to R5 as amended each have a passing focused test; N1 concerns the scope selection fix, which no requirement states.\"},\n{\"id\":\"scope\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"The nine code files match the spec artifact list; the lower-root selection change answers earlier findings and is stated in the spec API section and log.\"},\n{\"id\":\"security\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Changed names, including ../ forms, are only matched as strings in the code read, never opened; the versioned report interpolates nothing from Git.\"},\n{\"id\":\"solution-proportionality\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"A prefix lookup and a small rename function is proportionate; it holds only while the diff output form is fixed, the condition N1 breaks.\"}\n],\n\"tools\":[\n{\"id\":\"artifact-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose artifact-check --spec pose-validate-index-reads-residuals --strict\",\"rationale\":\"Exit 0.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-design\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"structure:design-eee831039bcb1105\",\"rationale\":\"Observed, no deltas.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-discover\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess discover --no-persist --component pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-integrate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/engine-reads-raw-history-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --no-persist.\"},\n{\"id\":\"assess-tech-debt\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose assess tech-debt --no-persist\",\"rationale\":\"The scan reports itself incomplete: two spec sources could not be read.\"},\n{\"id\":\"closeout-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose closeout-check spec:pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; cannot pass before the review is recorded and the spec is done.\"},\n{\"id\":\"review-check\",\"disposition\":\"deferred\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose review-check spec:pose-validate-index-reads-residuals\",\"rationale\":\"Ran; no fresh review record exists.\"},\n{\"id\":\"suggest-review\",\"component\":\"pose-mcp\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"command:pose suggest review --path pose-mcp\"},\n{\"id\":\"surface-check\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"integration:pose-mcp/go/delivery-integration\",\"rationale\":\"Ran with --strict: zero findings.\"},\n{\"id\":\"validate\",\"disposition\":\"passed\",\"evidence\":\"unit:pose-mcp/go/test\",\"rationale\":\"Rests on the sealed